{"id":"chatcmpl-1e09c32c-4647-4233-9ba3-ca8a074a9de2","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249591,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model corroboration strategy for medical image interpretation, where independent vision-language models are queried with targeted anatomical questions to resolve laterality ambiguity. The key insight is decomposing the diagnostic question into specific anatomical landmarks (fissures, chest wall) rather than asking for a direct answer, then cross-validating across models before committing to a final answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires distinguishing between left/right or other spatially ambiguous options, query models for anatomical landmarks and relative positions rather than asking directly for the answer.\",\n    \"Use two or more independent models/tools to corroborate a finding before finalizing, especially when the answer hinges on subtle spatial reasoning.\",\n    \"Decompose the original multiple-choice question into a descriptive sub-question that elicits supporting evidence (landmarks, relative locations) rather than a bare label.\",\n    \"Tailor the query to the specific imaging view (e.g., lateral vs. frontal) by referencing view-appropriate landmarks to disambiguate laterality.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Ask for anatomical landmarks and relative positions (fissures, walls, borders) instead of direct labels; corroborate with a second independent model.\",\n    \"Spatial/laterality disambiguation tasks\": \"Convert left/right choices into descriptive questions about position relative to known reference structures.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus decision-making\": \"Query independent tools with the same targeted sub-question and require agreement before committing to an answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the sub-question explicitly references view-appropriate anatomical landmarks that distinguish the candidate options.\",\n    \"Verify that at least two independent sources agree on the finding and laterality before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":501,"total_tokens":876,"completion_tokens":375,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":501},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":375}}}